// What is heard (s_sound.c, i_sound.c): the tic's sounds (`Sounds`) are
// played from the WAD's lumps, eight at a time at most. A thing or a
// sector is heard once at a time: its new sound cuts its old one off.
// Where all eight places are taken, a sound takes the place of one that
// matters no more than it does, or is not heard. While a sound lasts it
// follows what makes it: louder as that comes nearer, and from the side
// it is on then.
//
// The tune that is asked for (`Tune`) is played with them: its notes by
// music.ent on the chip of chip.ent, whose samples go to the device as
// they are made, as many each tic as it wants.
import files
import sound
import wad
import fixed
import level
import things
import play
import enemy
import sounds
import music
import chip

